  "rationale": "ADP‑Glo™ provides a homogeneous, luminescence‑based readout that directly measures kinase turnover of ATP to ADP, suitable for mTOR which is an ATP‑competitive target. The retained examples show that mTOR inhibition can be measured with peptide substrates (4E‑BP1) and 30‑min incubations, supporting the chosen substrate concentration and reaction time. A 3‑fold dilution series spanning 30 µM to ~0.02 µM captures the expected potency range for a selective ATP‑competitive inhibitor while keeping DMSO below 0.1 % to avoid enzyme artefacts. Replicates (n = 3) and the inclusion of a known inhibitor enable assessment of assay robustness and allow normalization of data.",
